# A World's place with a bundle answer, taken apart by a tuple pattern, whose constant
# field reads, as one value, a bundle a building `if` written below gives and one name
# binds whole, whose plain part is late (Semantics ch. 4, "Binding groups and cycles":
# any line may use any name the block binds, and "the order of a group's lines decides
# positions and nothing else"; ch. 8, "A new place's first value": the query answers at
# the build, by the element as built; Type System ch. 2, "Bundles": a bundle is a plain
# aggregate, so a name binds it and a function takes it; ruling TC). Nothing here is a
# cycle. Reaches `PreBindWhole`'s marker "the bundle `both`, whose plain part is late,
# read as one value at its block's build" on prismc-s4 (sweep-4's bootstrap of 076ee06b).
# Written by Claude (sweep-4, the prismc run), 12 November 2026; subject to change.
emit Ui.* | Pad.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

tag Pad.Port of Element ((Nat, $Text)):
    name: Text

First: fn ((Nat, !Click)) -> Nat
fn First ((k, ignore)) = k

@Page: fn Bool -> @unit
fn @Page loud:
    !add <- Ui.Button($label=$"add")                                   # 0
    ((p, $s)) <- Pad.Port(name="port {First both}")                    # 1
    Ui.Label($text=$"{p} {$s}")                                        # 2
    both <- if loud:
        Ui.Label($text=$"loud")                                        # 3
        @ ((10, !add))
    else:
        @ ((20, !add))
